<div class="card">
    <h2 class="card-header">Bridge 42 &ndash; NYMR &mdash; Site Introduction Briefing</h2>

    @foreach (var item in _sections)
    {
        <div class="medical-group">
            <h3 class="medical-group-title">@item.Title</h3>
            <div class="briefing-text">@item.Content</div>
        </div>
    }

    <div class="info-panel">
        <strong>Declaration:</strong> I confirm that I have received and understood the NYMR Bridge 42 Site Introduction Briefing and agree to comply with all site rules and safety requirements. I also accept that a separate briefing will be provided by CML before I am authorised to enter site or carry out any activity in relation to this project.
    </div>
    <div class="info-panel" style="background: var(--green-bg); border-color: var(--green); margin-top: 12px; font-style: italic;">
        "NYMR say Safety, respect for the local community, and protection of the railway asset are paramount. If in doubt, stop work and seek guidance from the Site Manager"
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    private readonly List<(string Title, string Content)> _sections =
    [
        ("Project Overview",
@"Project: Bridge 42 Temporary Propping Works
Location: Grosmont, North Yorkshire Moors Railway (NYMR)
Client: NYMR Trust
Main Contractor: Construction Marine LTD

Scope of Works:
• Installation of temporary propping to the brick arch intrados.
• River damming and construction of temporary foundations.
• Scaffolding and access installations.
• Crane operations for lifting and positioning of propping elements.
• Monitoring of bridge stability and levels.
• Associated site setup and reinstatement works.

The worksite is designated as a High Street Environment within a TIII Possession, meaning the railway is blocked to all train movements and under the control of the NYMR Engineering Supervisor (ES)."),

        ("Site Boundaries",
@"The limits of the worksite are clearly defined by:
• Heras fencing, and
• Existing stone parapet walls.
• Existing wooden boundary fencing.

Unauthorised access beyond these boundaries is strictly prohibited."),

        ("Access & Egress",
@"Access to and from the site is strictly controlled via:
1. South East Gate – pedestrian access via the public footpath.
2. South Level Crossing (Grosmont LX) Gates – for plant, deliveries, and emergency access.

All personnel must attend this induction and sign in and out of the site. Visitors and delivery vehicles must be escorted at all times."),

        ("Mandatory PPE",
@"• Safety helmet
• High-visibility clothing
• Safety boots
• Gloves
• Eye protection

Additional PPE (e.g., life jackets, harnesses, or hearing protection) must be worn as required by specific tasks."),

        ("Key Site Hazards",
@"• Working near water – risk of drowning; life-saving equipment provided.
• Lifting operations – obey exclusion zones and banksman instructions.
• Public interface – maintain vigilance near footpaths and local businesses.
• Heavy plant movements – follow designated routes and site speed limits.
• Structural stability – do not interfere with the bridge or propping system."),

        ("Track Safety Risk",
@"• Don't step on sleepers – risk of slips & falls, likely to be slippery especially when damp. Use ballast.
• Avoid Points and Point Rodding – risk of trips, falls, trapping of foot.
• Don't step on rails – risk of slips and falls.
• Don't move points – obey Engineering Supervisor instructions.
• Remain within the worksite or public areas – strictly no access to any other track or lineside area."),

        ("Emergency Arrangements",
@"• Emergency Services: Dial 999 or 112
• Assembly Point: Near the South East Gate
• Emergency Access Route: Via Grosmont Level Crossing

All accidents, incidents, and near misses must be reported immediately to the Site Manager."),

        ("Environmental Controls",
@"• Spill kits are available; report any pollution immediately.
• Waste must be disposed of in designated areas.
• Protect the river from contamination at all times.
• Respect the local community by minimising noise and disturbance."),

        ("Site Rules",
@"• The site operates as a controlled construction environment.
• Use of the local pub is strictly prohibited.
• No more than two workers are permitted in local shops at any one time to minimise disruption to the community.
• Smoking is not permitted anywhere on site.
• A designated smoking area is provided within the fenced compound in the car park, and this is the only location where smoking is allowed.
• Alcohol and drugs are strictly prohibited.
• Follow all instructions from the Engineering Supervisor and Site Manager.
• Maintain good housekeeping and respect neighbouring properties.")
    ];
}
